# Fleet map

If any of the first 5 non-empty lines of the user message (leading blank lines OK) is or begins with (case-insensitive) `Ти си <role>`, where `<role>` is Product, Code, Review, Release, Coord, installbot, or newproject (lowercase file name), read `.repo-rules/cursor/roles/<role lowercase>.md`, then `.repo-rules/common/`, then `docs/STATUS.md`, before doing anything.

- `docs/STATUS.md` — current snapshot (read first; wrap up the task here)
- `docs/memory/` — decisions, brand, handoff, open questions (`memory/bots/` = bot templates)
- `docs/architecture/` — system design, specs, catalogs, technical plans
- `docs/guides/` — PROJECT, TEAM, RISKS, how-tos, setup
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` — milestones and `Now`
- `docs/TASKS.md` — open tasks; **Code priorities** at the top = next Code work
- `docs/BRIEFS.md` — active Code briefs (started, not merged)
- `docs/HISTORY.md` — done log; open a matching row only
- Synced SHA: `.repo-rules/SYNCED_FROM`. Do not git pull in `.repo-rules/`. Private: commit `.repo-rules/` (do not gitignore). Public: gitignore `.repo-rules/` (local copy only).
